Hello!


Please update the regulatory rules for Russia (RU) on 5GHz to be the followi=
ng:

    (5170 - 5350 @ 40), (N/A, 20)
    (5650 - 5835 @ 40), (N/A, 30)

i.e. channels 34-64 can be used in either 20MHz or 40MHz modes with maximum p=
ower of 20dBm (-10 dBW), and channels 132-165 can be used in either 20MHz or=
 40MHz modes with maximum power of 30dBm (0 dBW).

Information is taken from the official document available here: http://www.r=
fs-rf.ru/idc/groups/public/documents/grhc_native_files/005571.doc
Rules for 2.4 GHz are not changed.


Best regards,
Roman A. aka BasicXP
